Chance-path buffs decided by the replay where the listing decided every cast's path (2026-11-26, Alesh's Rare Fin round).

What it does: replaycrits.ts chancePathBuff no longer leaves a buff on a chance jump's path (Alesh's P3 team ATK,
only on the Rare Fin's slam) to the log when castassembly.ts listedPaths / castsFromHitBuffs decided the path of
every cast of its skill (listedPathBuffs); the replay's own P3 instances are then judged against the listing.

Measured (`measure --at HEAD --base HEAD --patch <the revert of this>` with --with Alesh, on the code with the
listed paths and the listed cast): 0c14 plain 493 → 492, mismatch 12 → 9, damage −0.3 → −0.2%; a hold-out log
plain −47, assumed +13, fallback +33, mismatch +1 (hold-out plain 81.0 → 80.2%); nothing else moved.

Dropped: it gains nothing in development and costs one hold-out log 47 plain hits, which can't be diagnosed by hand.
What would have to change: whatever makes that log's replayed P3 disagree with its listing (its path decisions, or
the buff's clock: P3's 10 s under the hold placement); measure again after a round on the buff clock.

